# Python

- Harness package (`harness/sabot/`, `harness/pyproject.toml`): Python 3.11+. Runtime dependencies are empty. Scorers in `harness/scripts/score_*.py` stay Python 3.9+ and standard-library only.
- A new runtime dependency needs a one-line justification in the PR and a pinned lower bound in `harness/pyproject.toml`.
- Type hints on all public functions; `from __future__ import annotations` where the file already uses it.
- No bare `except:`. No `except Exception: pass` in any decision path. Raise specific exceptions.
- Deterministic by default: seed every RNG, sort dict/set iteration before hashing or printing, freeze timestamps in tests. The results field named `seed` is a replicate label, not an RNG seed.
- Secrets via `os.environ` only; never log secret values; never write them into `harness/runs/`.
- Use `pathlib`. No hard-coded absolute paths (no `/Users/...`).
